# Everyday CLI workflow

Read `specs/035-cli-everyday-lifecycle/spec.md` before changing CLI lifecycle
behavior.

## Source files

- Target resolution: `cli/src/workflow/target.rs`
- Process identity: `cli/src/workflow/instance.rs`
- Command dispatch: `cli/src/commands/workflow/`
- `up` / `down` / `logs` / status: `cli/src/workflow/lifecycle/`
- `kalam dev`: `cli/src/workflow/dev/`
- Canonical agent skill: `../kalamdb-skills/skills/kalamdb/references/cli-lifecycle.md`

## Invariants

- One resolved target for SQL, `dev`, `up`, `down`, `status`, and `logs`.
- `--global` / `-g` is shared-local (`~/.kalam/servers/default/`), not a
  network service.
- Reject `--global` with `--env`, `--url`, or `--host`.
- Do not treat a healthy port as ownership. Require `instance.json`.
- Honor existing `kalam/server` data paths; do not auto-migrate them.
- `link` must not silently change `project.default_env`.
- Do not inject root credentials into application processes.
- Ordinary schema-watch failures keep the database and app running.
- User-facing CLI changes also update `../kalamdb-skills`.
